  "summary_en": "Joint voluntary guidelines from the UK NCSC, US CISA and over 20 international partners for providers of AI systems. They set out secure-by-design practices across four life-cycle stages: design, development, deployment, and operation and maintenance. They focus on AI-specific vulnerabilities, supply chain security and incident management.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Security must be a core requirement throughout the AI system life cycle.",
   "Four stages: secure design, secure development, secure deployment, secure operation and maintenance.",
   "Providers should threat-model, secure the AI supply chain, and document data, models and prompts.",
   "Protect infrastructure and models, and put incident management processes in place.",
   "Aligned with secure-by-design principles, NCSC guidance and NIST SSDF."
